---
// Verbatim Authentic Content & Media from Khao Sok Riverside Cottages
import PageLayout from '../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

---

<PageLayout
  title="Elephant Sanctuary"
  description="Elephant Sanctuary Discover more with our Khao Sok FAQs"
  heroImage="/images/khao-sok-hero-cottages.jpg"
  heroTitle="Elephant Sanctuary"
  heroSubtitle="The Ancient Rainforest of Southern Thailand"
  breadcrumbs={[{"label": "Faq Category", "href": "/faq-category/"}, {"label": "Elephant Sanctuary", "href": "/faq-category/elephant-sanctuary/"}]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10">
    <div class="bg-[#faf8f5]/95 border border-[#12281b]/10 rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-8 md:p-12 shadow-2xl backdrop-blur-md">
      
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#12281b]/10 pb-4 mb-8 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-[#163824]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold">
          <span class="text-[#7a5813]">KSR</span>
          <span class="text-[#12281b]/20">/</span>
          <span>FIELD DISPATCH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="text-[#7a5813] font-bold">KHAO SOK · THAILAND</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[#223e2c] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">

        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>What are some of the benefits and the challenges of elephant tourism?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Benefits mean that elephants have found a new worth other than agriculture and work productivity, receiving better care than ever before. Challenges is ignorance of tourists around how elephants need to be treated, and the high costs of caring for elephants especially in a non-working setting.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>What do you like most about your job?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          We must stress that these elephants are domestic and raised by humans, so they cannot take care of themselves and do not know how to live in the wild. This means they must rely on humans for their care, which is a huge responsibility, but highly rewarding.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>What are some of the key things that you do with and for the elephants at the sanctuary?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          During the day the elephants are trained to be around people by visiting the tourists. They also get showered and bathed twice a day so that the careers can check them over for any cuts or injuries. At night, the elephants sleep in the forest where they can supplement their diets with jungle shrubs.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Can you tell me the story of an elephant in your care?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          One elephant came to them with a severe tetanus infection in her neck. Tetanus is not well studied in elephants so had to apply human care strategies. Also had to perform surgery to remove a large part of the infected area. The elephant is in full recovery now and showing no further signs of illness.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Why was the sanctuary opened?</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Firstly, it is not a sanctuary it is a conservation / rehabilitation center. The aim of the center is to support rehabilitation of DOMESTIC elephants in Thailand. The center was opened as a means of funding their veterinary hospital and clinic needs. They offer free elephant health care and advice to any owners of domestic elephants. Injured or sick elephants can stay at the center for an extended period, until they are returned to their owners, adopted by someone else OR surrendered to the center permanently. All of the funding for running the center, paying staff and running the hospital is generated through [...]
        </p>
      </div>

      
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
